PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
  "current_lean": "B",
  "confidence": "very-high",
  "round_developments": {
    "consensus": "Unanimous (6/6). All colleagues (including previously hesitant Colleagues 2 and 5) now firmly support Option B.",
    "key_arguments_solidified": [
      "Physical sorting mechanics & shear stress: BD FACSDiscover S8 images events upstream in the cuvette flow cell (CellView), but droplet break-off occurs downstream under ~70 psi nozzle shear stress. Genuine antigen-specific conjugates form tight, actin-dependent immunological synapses that withstand shear, whereas random, non-specific doublets dissociate in transit.",
      "Biological precursor frequency: Antigen-specific B cells against a specific tumor target in an unselected repertoire are exceptionally rare (<0.1%). Thus, double-positive imaged doublets are overwhelmingly coincidental collisions or weak adhesions.",
      "Binary outcome paradox vs. E: Nested degenerate BCR PCR amplifies any rearranged heavy and light chains with high efficiency if template is present. If 20 pg of tumor RNA or lysate suppressed SuperScript III in 5 µL, it would have suppressed all 95 wells. Instead, a stark binary outcome (4 crisp positive wells, 91 completely blank wells) proves template presence vs. template absence (i.e. no B cell landed in those 91 wells).",
      "Quantitative stoichiometry: A single tumor cell (~2–4 pL volume, 15–30 pg total RNA) in a 5 µL RT reaction represents a >10^6-fold volumetric dilution and is 5 orders of magnitude below SuperScript III capacity (up to 5 µg). Denaturation and RNase inhibitors in standard RT buffer prevent nuclease degradation, rendering E biochemically impossible."
    ],
    "distractor_status": [
      "A: Standard incubation time (40 min at 37°C + 30 min on ice) is adequate; misses biological precursor frequency.",
      "C: Claims conditions led to 'few doublets', contradicting the experimental fact that 95 doublet wells were successfully sorted.",
      "D: Mentions T-cell receptor 'alpha and beta chains' instead of B-cell heavy and light chains.",
      "E: Biochemically and stoichiometrically refuted by single-cell reaction parameters and binary PCR readout."
    ]
  },
  "next_step": "Maintain strong, concise defense of B through remaining deliberation rounds."
}

